WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.600
The Walking Dead has no shortage of bad&nbsp;
guys, big and small. But who's the biggest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.240
baddest antagonist of them all? We're&nbsp;
here to find out, by ranking every single&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.480
major Walking Dead villain from the least&nbsp;
impressive to the most brutally fearsome.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.720
First introduced in season seven, Jadis is the&nbsp;
leader of a faction known as the Scavengers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.880
Rick approaches them in the hopes of gaining&nbsp;
more soldiers in his fight against Negan and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:30.240
the Saviors. Jadis is depicted as a curt,&nbsp;
cold leader of a handful of loyal survivors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:34.480
She lives in a junkyard where she often makes&nbsp;
art out of the items that are discarded,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.480
and chooses to speak in broken English.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:43.840
"Still. Alone you. Need us to save you."

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.040
Although her eccentricities make Jadis,&nbsp;
whose real name is later revealed to be Anne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.200
irritating, they're not the reason she ranks&nbsp;
as one of the worst villains on the show.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:58.000
When push comes to shove, Jadis' move is always&nbsp;
to extort something out of the people she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.200
has power over. When Rick comes with his hat in&nbsp;
his hand, she demands some kind of tribute. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:08.880
she agrees to fight alongside him, she eventually&nbsp;
betrays the Alexandrians and joins the Saviors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.840
only to later betray them when&nbsp;
the tide of the battle shifts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:17.520
In the end, she makes one greedy choice too&nbsp;
many, and her entire group is massacred by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.280
the Saviors at the behest of Simon.&nbsp;
Her time as a villain is marked by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:25.840
perplexing character traits and an inability&nbsp;
to really impact the outcome of the world.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:30.320
When Gregory is introduced, he&nbsp;
seems like an impressive figure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.760
He's run the Hilltop colony since the beginning,&nbsp;
and by season six it stands as one of the few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:40.880
safe havens left in the world. However, as&nbsp;
the world grows and alliances start to form,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.840
it becomes clear that Gregory is only a peacetime&nbsp;
leader — and a very average one at that.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.800
When the Saviors first arrive, he's unable to&nbsp;
put up much of a fight and almost immediately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:55.760
rolls over. Once Rick comes around, he&nbsp;
realizes that his people need some muscle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.240
and agrees to help, right up until Rick&nbsp;
loses his first battle with the Saviors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:05.040
He then declares their deal null and void.&nbsp;
After that, Maggie gains popularity as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.600
leader among Hilltop residents, prompting&nbsp;
Gregory to attempt to defect to the Saviors.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:13.840
Perhaps you've already noticed the pattern&nbsp;
here: Gregory gives up at the drop of a hat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:18.640
Whenever things get real, he simply quits and&nbsp;
joins the other team, bouncing back and forth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:22.800
between the good guys and bad guys and&nbsp;
having little impact on either faction.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.520
"You really gonna stand there and&nbsp;
pretend you didn't try to sell us out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.840
sell this place out? To the saviors?"

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.200
"I was working for the side of&nbsp;
sanity. I was working for peace."

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.320
Hero or villain, a person in the world&nbsp;
of The Walking Dead has to make big moves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:40.960
that might lead to conflict. Even if he's&nbsp;
no fighter, maintaining control is key,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:45.280
and Gregory, from the get-go, never&nbsp;
really has control of anyone or anything.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.320
It's rare that a villainous group on&nbsp;
The Walking Dead has no distinct leader,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:54.640
but such is the case with the Wolves. The&nbsp;
Wolves are a group of marauders active in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:59.440
the Washington D.C. area who survive by&nbsp;
raiding any living people for supplies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:04.000
then using their zombified bodies as bait&nbsp;
to attract more prey. They foster a sense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:10.000
of unease in the area by marking areas they've hit&nbsp;
with the words "Wolves not far." Their theatrics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:15.600
don't end there: They carve a "W" into both their&nbsp;
foreheads and the foreheads of their victims.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:19.680
For all their style, the Wolves don't&nbsp;
last very long against Rick's group…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.800
or even Carol on her own. In season six,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:28.560
after teasing their presence in the area for&nbsp;
weeks, they launch a full-on attack on Alexandria.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:33.360
In the end, however, their attack on Alexandria&nbsp;
is nothing more than a surprisingly toothless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:38.480
display of intimidation. Carol, disguised as a&nbsp;
Wolf, successfully slaughters a number of them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:43.680
and the Alexandrians are able to repel their&nbsp;
forces. So much for the Wolves' ferocity.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:48.280
"You said it, right? Don't ever be sorry."

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:54.480
All things considered, Gareth is actually a pretty&nbsp;
savvy villain. Not only does he lead a large&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:59.040
faction of people, he manages to hatch a pretty&nbsp;
clever scheme that brings a lot of unsuspecting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:04.720
victims into his web. After founding Terminus as&nbsp;
a safe haven, Gareth's good intentions are foiled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:09.840
by a group of hostile survivors who briefly&nbsp;
take over. He manages to get the place back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:14.960
but only by resorting to villainous tactics.&nbsp;
Following this, Gareth grows merciless and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:19.520
turns his little beacon of hope into a&nbsp;
trap for people in the area who hear radio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:24.960
broadcasts hailing Terminus as a sanctuary.&nbsp;
In reality, it's a meat factory for cannibals.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:30.800
"If it makes you feel any better, you taste&nbsp;
much better than we thought you would."

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:36.720
The only reason Gareth ranks so low on this&nbsp;
list is simply that his villainy doesn't last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:41.040
long in the face of Rick Grimes and his&nbsp;
survivors. After Gareth captures the group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.720
and attempts to slaughter them for&nbsp;
meat, Rick and company manage to escape&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.840
and take Terminus out. With&nbsp;
everything he built in ruins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:53.200
Gareth tracks them to a nearby church and manages&nbsp;
to capture Bob. Ultimately, though, his tracking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:58.240
amounts to nothing as Rick makes good on his&nbsp;
promise to kill him with a red-handled machete.

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:02.240
Gareth is neither the most cunning, nor the&nbsp;
most threatening villain on The Walking Dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.120
but he does manage to build&nbsp;
something worthy of infamy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:08.000
Unfortunately, his contribution&nbsp;
to the world ends there.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:11.840
Dwight is an enormously&nbsp;
complicated villain. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:15.760
that complexity somewhat diminishes&nbsp;
his level of success as a bad guy:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:20.960
His heart just isn't in it. Dwight is introduced&nbsp;
as someone who betrays Daryl's kindness on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:26.720
road after fleeing the Saviors with his wife and&nbsp;
sister-in-law. Eventually, the family returns,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:32.400
and Negan separates Dwight from his wife and burns&nbsp;
half his face off with an iron for his desertion.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:37.200
After enduring this trauma and spending a&nbsp;
good portion of time in solitary confinement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:42.000
Dwight emerges as one of Negan's top guys.&nbsp;
He's reintroduced to the survivors after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:45.520
he mercilessly shoots Denise through&nbsp;
the eye, and is part of the team that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:50.240
captures the survivors before Abraham and&nbsp;
Glenn are executed by Negan. Basically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:54.000
Dwight is an irredeemable bastard&nbsp;
at this point in the story. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:58.880
his love for his wife keeps a singular spark&nbsp;
of humanity alive within him, and eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:03.920
he makes the bold choice to turn on Negan and the&nbsp;
Saviors and act as a mole for the Alexandrians.

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:08.640
"I hate him. I hate Negan."

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:14.880
For a time, Dwight is a pretty captivating figure&nbsp;
to watch, because it's genuinely unclear where his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:20.400
loyalties lie. In the end, he makes the tough call&nbsp;
to do the right thing, and Daryl spares his life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:25.280
as a result. He's one of The Walking Dead's&nbsp;
more understated antagonists, and that makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:30.400
him a relatively minor figure on this list, but&nbsp;
definitely not in the hearts of the show's fans.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:36.400
While Joe never leads a large group like Jadis,&nbsp;
Gareth, or the Wolves, he gets major points&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:41.200
for being a seriously evil person. He's first&nbsp;
introduced as the leader of a very small group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:46.480
of marauders called the Claimers. They roll into&nbsp;
a house that Rick happens to be hiding out in and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:52.160
quickly demonstrate their depravity. Rick manages&nbsp;
to escape them, but not without killing a Claimer.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:56.800
While tracking Rick down for revenge, Joe&nbsp;
meets and befriends Daryl and explains his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:02.320
philosophy on leadership. Joe manages to keep his&nbsp;
small group in line by issuing one major rule:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:06.960
Anyone who claims something owns it by right.&nbsp;
Those who violate this rule are punished with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:11.520
a beating, "or worse." The Claimers are&nbsp;
a small faction because Joe deals with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:15.360
internal conflicts by straight-up&nbsp;
killing the person who is at fault.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:20.560
When Joe catches up to Rick, he threatens to&nbsp;
kill Daryl and assault both Michonne and Carl.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:23.760
He genuinely gets one over&nbsp;
on Rick, but only briefly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:28.160
because Joe underestimates his opponent's&nbsp;
savagery. Rick rips out Joe's throat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:32.080
with his teeth, putting an end to his&nbsp;
misguided worldview right then and there.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.640
"Fell apart? I never looked at it like that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:41.840
Seems to me things are finally starting&nbsp;
to fall together. Least for guys like us."

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:46.800
Sometimes, the scariest villains are the&nbsp;
ones who are convinced they're the good guy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:50.320
When Dawn is introduced, she's&nbsp;
several years into the apocalypse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:53.280
but is still holding out&nbsp;
hope for a government rescue.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:57.120
Dawn presides over a hospital that&nbsp;
she and a handful of other survivors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:02.960
cops, and physicians have turned into a very tense&nbsp;
safe haven. With resources dwindling, Dawn allows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:07.840
all sorts of horrific crimes, all in the name of&nbsp;
keeping their way of life going until a government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:13.760
rescue arrives. This is, as the audience knows,&nbsp;
a long wait for a train that simply isn't coming.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:15.440
"Try to look at the good we're doing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:21.760
Hard as it was, we saved Joan's life.&nbsp;
Trevett's life. We saved your life."

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:27.680
When Beth arrives as a patient, she's given a&nbsp;
crash course in Dawn's deeply and profoundly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:33.040
misguided way of leading. When Beth befriends a&nbsp;
guy named Noah, they hatch a plan that half-fails,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:37.680
and only allows him to escape. While Beth stays&nbsp;
back and faces the consequences from one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:43.280
Dawn's men, it becomes clear that Dawn is losing&nbsp;
control, prompting her to do something drastic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:46.960
When Beth's group comes to negotiate a&nbsp;
trade for Beth and Carol, who has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:50.960
injured and brought to the hospital, Dawn&nbsp;
tries to prove herself by demanding they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:56.160
get Noah back as well. Driven to madness by&nbsp;
her brief time with Dawn, Beth stabs her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:59.840
Dawn reflexively shoots her, and&nbsp;
is immediately shot dead by Daryl.

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:06.320
The Governor, AKA Philip Blake, deserves high&nbsp;
honors for being The Walking Dead's very first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:10.640
through-and-through, honest-to-God villain.&nbsp;
Prior to his arrival, the worst threat to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:16.080
humanity is Merle Dixon. When Daryl's brother is&nbsp;
finally seen again after more than a year, he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:20.640
following the Governor's orders — which really&nbsp;
says something about the company Blake keeps.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:25.120
When the Governor is introduced, he is revealed&nbsp;
to have accomplished what Rick has failed to do:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:29.440
He has created a working society within&nbsp;
the zombie apocalypse. While the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:34.080
has since seen a bevy of strongholds from&nbsp;
both good guys and bad guys take shape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:38.640
the Governor is the first to do it.&nbsp;
It's not exactly a success, however:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:44.000
Things get very dystopian there only about a&nbsp;
year or two out from the onset of the apocalypse.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:48.080
"You know all about me and I know all&nbsp;
about you. I don't care about any of that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:49.840
We're here to move forward."

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:55.520
What really makes the Governor a&nbsp;
top villain isn't his leadership,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.520 --> 00:10:00.240
but his madness. There's just no telling how&nbsp;
he'll wield his power from moment to moment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:04.800
Even his demise comes as a result of his&nbsp;
own lunacy. Upset over the loss of Woodbury&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:09.520
and its people's assimilation into the prison,&nbsp;
he drives a tank through one of the only safe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:14.400
havens left in the world, and dies trying&nbsp;
to exact physical revenge on Rick Grimes.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:21.120
Alpha is curt, cold, and has no time for any&nbsp;
weakness in her ranks. She survives by leading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:25.600
a group called the Whisperers, who live among&nbsp;
the walkers and even manage to control their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:30.480
movements through herding tactics. She is the&nbsp;
first to recognize that the walkers are the weapon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:35.680
that brought humanity to its knees, making even&nbsp;
the mightiest people and institutions fall. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:39.920
when she encounters Rick's group, she has&nbsp;
very little time for their emotionality and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:43.440
moral compunctions. However, since&nbsp;
they've captured her only daughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:47.040
Lydia, she has no choice but to roll&nbsp;
through them with brutal vengeance.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:52.240
The war with the Whisperers becomes one of the&nbsp;
strongest conflicts in the series. Though Beta,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:57.200
Alpha's right-hand man, does most of the heavy&nbsp;
lifting, she's the one who herds enough walkers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.200 --> 00:11:01.920
to basically wield this world's equivalent of a&nbsp;
nuke. Alpha is one of very few villains on The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:06.480
Walking Dead who doesn't underestimate her&nbsp;
opponents, and that counts for everything.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:11.800
"They all follow me by choice.&nbsp;
Cause I make em strong."

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:17.200
Even people with a cursory understanding&nbsp;
of The Walking Dead know that Negan is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:21.680
greatest antagonist the show has ever seen.&nbsp;
Although he spends a majority of his time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:26.720
on the show on a path to redemption, he wouldn't&nbsp;
even be alive if it wasn't for his ruthlessness.

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:32.080
When Negan is first introduced, he infamously&nbsp;
kills Abraham and Glenn for no other reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:36.880
than to demonstrate his power. Negan has a&nbsp;
twisted way of always making "good" decisions:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:41.040
He views people as a resource. This&nbsp;
means he's not a loose cannon homicidal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:45.280
maniac like the Governor or Joe — his&nbsp;
conflicts are calculated, and he knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:49.760
who will live or die before he even begins&nbsp;
a conversation. When it comes to leadership,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:54.640
he differs from Jadis and Dawn in that he&nbsp;
knows success lies not in keeping people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:59.920
going, but in giving them an opportunity to&nbsp;
thrive, hence the Sanctuary's point system.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:07.920
"Let Mark's face be a daily reminder to him&nbsp;
and to everyone else that the rules matter."

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:11.920
However, the main thing that makes&nbsp;
Negan such an effective villain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:16.560
is the fact that he's capable. Unlike&nbsp;
Gregory or Dawn, when push comes to shove,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:21.440
Negan can fend for himself. He boasts the&nbsp;
smartest and most broken mind in any room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:25.280
and is enormously capable of exerting&nbsp;
his will on the people around him.

